The MIT terms above cover the code in `src/`, `tests/` and `scripts/`.

They do not cover the data. `data/manifest.csv`, `results/` and
`taxonomy/` derive from AfriSpeech-200 (intronhealth/afrispeech-200), which is
licensed CC-BY-NC-SA-4.0. Those files inherit the same terms: attribution,
non-commercial use, share-alike. No dataset audio is distributed here.

Olatunji et al., AfriSpeech-200: Pan-African Accented Speech Dataset for
Clinical and General Domain ASR, arXiv:2310.00274.
